  23:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   ==============================================================================
  24:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                         ##### PWR peripheral overview #####
  25:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   ==============================================================================
  26:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   [..]
  27:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) The Power control (PWR) provides an overview of the supply architecture
  28:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        for the different power domains and of the supply configuration
  29:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        controller.
  30:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        In the H7 family, the number of power domains is different between
  31:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        device lines. This difference is due to characteristics of each device.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\HUAV\AppData\Local\Temp\ccoKuDbb.s 			page 2


  32:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
  33:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Domain architecture overview for the different H7 lines:
  34:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Dual core lines are STM32H745, STM32H747, STM32H755 and STM32H757.
  35:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           These devices have 3 power domains (D1, D2 and D3).
  36:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           The domain D1 contains a CPU (Cortex-M7), a Flash memory and some
  37:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           peripherals. The D2 domain contains peripherals and a CPU
  38:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (Cortex-M4). The D3 domain contains the system control, I/O logic
  39:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           and low-power peripherals.
  40:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) STM32H72x, STM32H73x, STM32H742, STM32H743, STM32H750 and STM32H753 
  41:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           devices have 3 power domains (D1, D2 and D3).
  42:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           The domain D1 contains a CPU (Cortex-M7), a Flash memory and some
  43:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           peripherals. The D2 domain contains peripherals. The D3 domains
  44:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           contains the system control, I/O logic and low-power peripherals.
  45:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) STM32H7Axxx and STM32H7Bxxx devices have 2 power domains (CD and SRD).
  46:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           The core domain (CD) contains a CPU (Cortex-M7), a Flash
  47:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           memory and peripherals. The SmartRun domain contains the system
  48:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           control, I/O logic and low-power peripherals.
  49:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
  50:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Every entity have low power mode as described below :
  51:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) The CPU low power modes are :
  52:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) CPU CRUN.
  53:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) CPU CSLEEP.
  54:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) CPU CSTOP.
  55:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) The domain low power modes are :
  56:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) DRUN.
  57:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) DSTOP.
  58:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) DSTANDBY.
  59:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) The SYSTEM low power modes are :
  60:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) RUN* : The Run* mode is entered after a POR reset and a wakeup from
  61:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                  Standby. In Run* mode, the performance is limited and the
  62:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                  system supply configuration shall be programmed. The system
  63:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                  enters Run mode only when the ACTVOSRDY bit in PWR control
  64:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                  status register 1 (PWR_CSR1) is set to 1.
  65:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) RUN.
  66:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) STOP.
  67:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) STANDBY.
  68:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
  69:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   ==============================================================================
  70:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  71:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   ==============================================================================
  72:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   [..]
  73:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Power management peripheral is active by default at startup level in
  74:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        STM32h7xx lines.
  75:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
  76:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_EnableBkUpAccess() and HAL_PWR_DisableBkUpAccess() functions
  77:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        to enable/disable access to the backup domain (RTC registers, RTC backup
  78:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        data registers and backup SRAM).
  79:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
  80:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_ConfigPVD() after setting parameters to be configured (event
  81:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        mode and voltage threshold) in order to set up the Power Voltage Detector,
  82:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        then use HAL_PWR_EnablePVD() and  HAL_PWR_DisablePVD() functions to start
  83:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        and stop the PVD detection.
  84:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        (+) PVD level could be one of the following values :
  85:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****              (++) 1V95
  86:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****              (++) 2V1
  87:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****              (++) 2V25
  88:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****              (++) 2V4
ARM GAS  C:\Users\HUAV\AppData\Local\Temp\ccoKuDbb.s 			page 3


  89:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****              (++) 2V55
  90:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****              (++) 2V7
  91:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****              (++) 2V85
  92:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****              (++) External voltage level
  93:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
  94:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_EnableWakeUpPin() and HAL_PWR_DisableWakeUpPin() functions
  95:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        with the right parameter to configure the wake up pin polarity (Low or
  96:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        High) and to enable and disable it.
  97:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
  98:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_EnterSLEEPMode() function to enter the current Core in SLEEP
  99:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        mode. Wake-up from SLEEP mode could be following to an event or an
 100:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        interrupt according to low power mode intrinsic request called (__WFI()
 101:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        or __WFE()).
 102:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        Please ensure to clear all CPU pending events by calling
 103:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        HAL_PWREx_ClearPendingEvent() function when trying to enter the Cortex-Mx
 104:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        in SLEEP mode with __WFE() entry.
 105:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 106:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_EnterSTOPMode() function to enter the whole system to Stop 0
 107:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        mode for single core devices. For dual core devices, this API will enter
 108:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        the domain (containing Cortex-Mx that executing this function) in DSTOP
 109:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        mode. According to the used parameter, user could select the regulator to
 110:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        be kept actif in low power mode and wake-up event type.
 111:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        Please ensure to clear all CPU pending events by calling
 112:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        HAL_PWREx_ClearPendingEvent() function when trying to enter the Cortex-Mx
 113:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        in CSTOP mode with __WFE() entry.
 114:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 115:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_EnterSTANDBYMode() function to enter the whole system in
 116:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        STANDBY mode for single core devices. For dual core devices, this API
 117:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        will enter the domain (containing Cortex-Mx that executing this function)
 118:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        in DSTANDBY mode.
 119:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 120:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_EnableSleepOnExit() and HAL_PWR_DisableSleepOnExit() APIs to
 121:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        enable and disable the Cortex-Mx re-entring in SLEEP mode after an
 122:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        interruption handling is over.
 123:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 124:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_EnableSEVOnPend() and HAL_PWR_DisableSEVOnPend() functions
 125:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        to configure the Cortex-Mx to wake-up after any pending event / interrupt
 126:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        even if it's disabled or has insufficient priority to cause exception
 127:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        entry.
 128:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 129:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    (#) Call HAL_PWR_PVD_IRQHandler() function to handle the PWR PVD interrupt
 130:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        request.
 131:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 132:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****      *** PWR HAL driver macros list ***
 133:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****      =============================================
 134:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****      [..]
 135:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        Below the list of most used macros in PWR HAL driver.
 136:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 137:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) __HAL_PWR_VOLTAGESCALING_CONFIG() : Configure the main internal
