 262:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================
 263:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                  ##### Peripheral Control Functions #####
 264:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****  ===============================================================================
 265:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 266:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       This section provides functions allowing to control power peripheral.
 267:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 268:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     *** PVD configuration ***
 269:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     =========================
 270:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 271:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) The PVD is used to monitor the VDD power supply by comparing it to a
 272:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           threshold selected by the PVD Level (PLS[7:0] bits in the PWR_CR1
 273:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           register).
 274:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 275:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) A PVDO flag is available to indicate if VDD is higher or lower
 276:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           than the PVD threshold. This event is internally connected to the EXTI
 277:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           line 16 to generate an interrupt if enabled.
 278:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           It is configurable through __HAL_PWR_PVD_EXTI_ENABLE_IT() macro.
 279:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 280:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) The PVD is stopped in STANDBY mode.
 281:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 282:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     *** Wake-up pin configuration ***
 283:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     =================================
 284:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 285:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Wake-up pin is used to wake up the system from STANDBY mode.
 286:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           The pin pull is configurable through the WKUPEPR register to be in
 287:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           No-pull, Pull-up and Pull-down.
 288:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           The pin polarity is configurable through the WKUPEPR register to be
 289:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           active on rising or falling edges.
 290:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 291:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) There are up to six Wake-up pin in the STM32H7 devices family.
 292:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 293:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     *** Low Power modes configuration ***
 294:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     =====================================
 295:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 296:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****      The device present 3 principles low-power modes features:
 297:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) SLEEP mode   : Cortex-Mx is stopped and all PWR domains are remaining
 298:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                          active (Powered and Clocked).
 299:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 300:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) STOP mode    : Cortex-Mx is stopped, clocks are stopped and the
 301:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                          regulator is running. The Main regulator or the LP
 302:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                          regulator could be selected.
 303:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 304:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) STANDBY mode : All PWR domains enter DSTANDBY mode and the VCORE
 305:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****                          supply regulator is powered off.
 306:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 307:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    *** SLEEP mode ***
 308:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    ==================
 309:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 310:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 311:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****         The SLEEP mode is entered by using the HAL_PWR_EnterSLEEPMode(Regulator,
ARM GAS  C:\Users\HUAV\AppData\Local\Temp\ccoKuDbb.s 			page 9


 312:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****         SLEEPEntry) function.
 313:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 314:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_SLEEPENTRY_WFI: enter SLEEP mode with WFI instruction.
 315:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (++) PWR_SLEEPENTRY_WFE: enter SLEEP mode with WFE instruction.
 316:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 317:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       -@@- The Regulator parameter is not used for the STM32H7 family
 318:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****               and is kept as parameter just to maintain compatibility with the
 319:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****               lower power families (STM32L).
 320:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 321:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 322:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****         Any peripheral interrupt acknowledged by the nested vectored interrupt
 323:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****         controller (NVIC) can wake up the device from SLEEP mode.
 324:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 325:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    *** STOP mode ***
 326:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    =================
 327:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 328:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       In system STOP mode, all clocks in the 1.2V domain are stopped, the PLL,
 329:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       the HSI, and the HSE RC oscillators are disabled. Internal SRAM and
 330:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       register contents are preserved.
 331:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The voltage regulator can be configured either in normal or low-power mode.
 332:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       To minimize the consumption in STOP mode, FLASH can be powered off before
 333:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       entering the STOP mode using the HAL_PWREx_EnableFlashPowerDown() function.
 334:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       It can be switched on again by software after exiting the STOP mode using
 335:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       the HAL_PWREx_DisableFlashPowerDown() function.
 336:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 337:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Entry:
 338:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****          The STOP mode is entered using the HAL_PWR_EnterSTOPMode(Regulator,
 339:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****          STOPEntry) function with:
 340:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 341:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****          (++) Regulator:
 342:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (+++) PWR_MAINREGULATOR_ON: Main regulator ON.
 343:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (+++) PWR_LOWPOWERREGULATOR_ON: Low Power regulator ON.
 344:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 345:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****          (++) STOPEntry:
 346:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (+++) PWR_STOPENTRY_WFI: enter STOP mode with WFI instruction.
 347:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****           (+++) PWR_STOPENTRY_WFE: enter STOP mode with WFE instruction.
 348:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 349:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (+) Exit:
 350:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****          Any EXTI Line (Internal or External) configured in Interrupt/Event mode.
 351:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 352:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    *** STANDBY mode ***
 353:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    ====================
 354:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 355:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     (+)
 356:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The system STANDBY mode allows to achieve the lowest power consumption.
 357:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       It is based on the Cortex-Mx deep SLEEP mode, with the voltage regulator
 358:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       disabled. The system is consequently powered off. The PLL, the HSI
 359:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       oscillator and the HSE oscillator are also switched off. SRAM and register
 360:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       contents are lost except for the RTC registers, RTC backup registers,
 361:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       backup SRAM and standby circuitry.
 362:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 363:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 364:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       The voltage regulator is OFF.
 365:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 366:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (++) Entry:
 367:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****         (+++) The STANDBY mode is entered using the HAL_PWR_EnterSTANDBYMode()
 368:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****               function.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\HUAV\AppData\Local\Temp\ccoKuDbb.s 			page 10


 369:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 370:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****       (++) Exit:
 371:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****         (+++) WKUP pin rising or falling edge, RTC alarm (Alarm A and Alarm B),
 372:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****               RTC wakeup, tamper event, time stamp event, external reset in NRST
 373:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****               pin, IWDG reset.
 374:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 375:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    *** Auto-wakeup (AWU) from low-power mode ***
 376:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****    =============================================
 377:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****     [..]
 378:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****      (+) The MCU can be woken up from low-power mode by an RTC Alarm event, an
 379:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****          RTC Wakeup event, a tamper event or a time-stamp event, without
 380:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****          depending on an external interrupt (Auto-wakeup mode).
 381:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 382:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****      (+) RTC auto-wakeup (AWU) from the STOP and STANDBY modes
 383:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 384:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        (++) To wake up from the STOP mode with an RTC alarm event, it is
 385:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****             necessary to configure the RTC to generate the RTC alarm using the
 386:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****             HAL_RTC_SetAlarm_IT() function.
 387:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 388:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        (++) To wake up from the STOP mode with an RTC Tamper or time stamp event,
 389:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****             it is necessary to configure the RTC to detect the tamper or time
 390:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****             stamp event using the HAL_RTCEx_SetTimeStamp_IT() or
 391:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****             HAL_RTCEx_SetTamper_IT() functions.
 392:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 393:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****        (++) To wake up from the STOP mode with an RTC WakeUp event, it is
 394:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****             necessary to configure the RTC to generate the RTC WakeUp event
 395:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****             using the HAL_RTCEx_SetWakeUpTimer_IT() function.
 396:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 397:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** @endverbatim
 398:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @{
 399:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   */
 400:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** 
 401:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c **** /**
 402:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @brief  Configure the event mode and the voltage threshold detected by the
 403:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         Programmable Voltage Detector(PVD).
 404:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @param  sConfigPVD : Pointer to an PWR_PVDTypeDef structure that contains
 405:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *                      the configuration information for the PVD.
 406:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note   Refer to the electrical characteristics of your device datasheet for
 407:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         more details about the voltage threshold corresponding to each
 408:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         detection level.
 409:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note   For dual core devices, please ensure to configure the EXTI lines for
 410:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         the different Cortex-Mx through PWR_Exported_Macro provided by this
