 676:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         Cortex-Mx that executing this function) in DSTANDBY mode. If all
 677:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         Cortex-Mx domains are in DSTANDBY and RUN_D3 bit in CPUCR register
 678:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         is cleared, all the system will enter in STANDBY mode.
 679:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note   The system enters Standby mode only when all domains are in DSTANDBY.
 680:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note   When the System exit STANDBY mode by issuing an interrupt or a
 681:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         wakeup event, the HSI RC oscillator is selected as system clock.
 682:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @note   It is recommended to disable all regulators before entring STANDBY
 683:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   *         mode for power consumption saving purpose.
 684:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   * @retval None.
 685:HW_Lib/STM32H7/HAL_Lib/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h7xx_hal_pwr.c ****   */
